reporter.raw:
{
  "single_story": {
    "yes": true,
    "note": "All sources cover the Oct 6, 2026 Mistral Large 4 ('Le Chonk') preview launch."
  },
  "the_news": {
    "text": "On Oct 6, 2026, French AI lab Mistral released a public preview of Mistral Large 4 ('Le Chonk'), a 1-trillion-parameter model it says is the strongest open-weight model outside China, with weights due by end of October.",
    "ids": [
      "F1",
      "F2",
      "F3",
      "F4"
    ]
  },
  "why_it_matters": [
    {
      "text": "Mistral pitches the model as an ownable alternative to closed US models, which the US government has restricted, and to Chinese open models; independent benchmarking so far places it below top US flagships but well ahead of the best US open-weight model.",
      "ids": [
        "F5",
        "F8",
        "F9",
        "F12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Mistral frames cyberdefense as a key use case, arguing closed models may refuse security tasks or lose access mid-incident.",
      "ids": [
        "F10",
        "F11"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "text": "Mistral launched a public preview of Mistral Large 4 (ML4), nicknamed 'Le Chonk', on Oct 6, 2026, available via API on Mistral Studio.",
      "sources": [
        "Mistral AI blog",
        "WIRED",
        "TechCrunch",
        "The Register"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "text": "ML4 is a 1 trillion-parameter, natively multimodal mixture-of-experts model with 49 billion active parameters.",
      "sources": [
        "Mistral AI blog",
        "The Register"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "NewsCord (aggregator) says 1.05 trillion total; not used as sole source."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "text": "Weights are not yet released: Mistral says they will drop by the end of October (NewsCord, an aggregator, says Oct 27); until then it is red-teaming the model with cybersecurity leaders, vetted partners and state authorities, who get a version with reduced moderation and expanded cyber capabilities.",
      "sources": [
        "Mistral AI blog",
        "WIRED",
        "The Register"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "TechCrunch says 'in just three weeks' and that it is 'not an open-weight model yet', accessible via a public guardrail endpoint."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "text": "[CLAIM: Mistral says] ML4 is state-of-the-art among open models on cybersecurity, finance and law, competitive with the strongest open-source models globally, and significantly outperforms any open-weight model from the US or Europe.",
      "sources": [
        "Mistral AI blog",
        "WIRED"
      ],
      "claim_by": "Mistral",
      "notes": [
        "WIRED: Mistral presents it as by far the most capable open-weight model developed outside China and 'very, very close' to some proprietary models."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F5",
      "text": "Independent benchmarker Artificial Analysis' early testing places ML4 preview on its intelligence leaderboard between DeepSeek V4.1 Flash and OpenAI's entry-level GPT6 Luna, at a major disadvantage to OpenAI and Anthropic flagships, but well ahead of the top US open-weights model, Thinking Machines Lab's Inkling.",
      "sources": [
        "The Register"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "Single-source (Register's description of Artificial Analysis results). The Register says Mistral's own benchmarks tell a 'far rosier' story and advises a grain of salt. TechCrunch notes benchmark results are still pending."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F6",
      "text": "[CLAIM: Mistral says] ML4 was trained from scratch on 3,800 NVIDIA Grace Blackwell GPUs in its own European datacenters, on data spanning more than 160 languages.",
      "sources": [
        "Mistral AI blog",
        "The Register"
      ],
      "claim_by": "Mistral",
      "notes": [
        "TechCrunch (quoting Pierre Stock) and WIRED-aggregator NewsCord say about 4,000 GPUs; Stock says this is two to three times fewer than Chinese competitors. NewsCord says two months of training."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F7",
      "text": "WIRED reports Chinese labs have been accused by the US government of abusing distillation, whereas Mistral claims it trained its model from scratch.",
      "sources": [
        "WIRED"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "Training-from-scratch claim is Mistral's."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F8",
      "text": "[CLAIM: Mistral says] On the Artificial Analysis Cyber Index ML4 ranks in the top five models globally and leads non-Chinese open-weight models by a wide margin; it scores 82% on a vulnerability reproduce-and-patch test and 93% on Cybench.",
      "sources": [
        "Mistral AI blog"
      ],
      "claim_by": "Mistral",
      "notes": [
        "Mistral says Claude Opus 5.5 and GPT-6 Astra score near zero on the test because they refuse. The Register repeats that Mistral claims strong cyber performance."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F9",
      "text": "Mistral says it ranks second of five in a blind human coding evaluation by Surge AI (3.74), behind only Claude Opus 5 (4.22).",
      "sources": [
        "Mistral AI blog"
      ],
      "claim_by": "Mistral",
      "notes": [
        "Mistral-reported; the evaluation was commissioned by Mistral per the blog's wording ('we ran')."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F10",
      "text": "Mistral argues provider-level refusals can block legitimate vulnerability research, and losing access to a capability mid-incident can itself be a security risk.",
      "sources": [
        "Mistral AI blog",
        "The Register"
      ],
      "claim_by": "Mistral",
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "F11",
      "text": "Mistral says ML4 is optimized for coding, cyberdefense and niche domains like manufacturing, finance and electrical engineering; TechCrunch adds chip design, relevant to backers ASML and Samsung.",
      "sources": [
        "WIRED",
        "TechCrunch"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "F12",
      "text": "WIRED reports that in June the Trump administration placed temporary restrictions on distribution of OpenAI and Anthropic models over cyberattack concerns, creating an opening for Mistral's open-weight models.",
      "sources": [
        "WIRED"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "Single-source."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "F13",
      "text": "Mistral says ML4 is the first milestone funded by its €3 billion Series D, which it calls the largest equity round ever raised by a European technology company; it expects large improvements in coming weeks and months as RL training continues.",
      "sources": [
        "Mistral AI blog",
        "The Register"
      ],
      "claim_by": "Mistral",
      "notes": [
        "WIRED gives the September round as $3.3 billion at a $24 billion valuation, the largest ever raise by a European tech company; TechCrunch says Samsung led the Series D at €21 billion valuation (about $24.39 billion)."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "background": [
    {
      "id": "B1",
      "text": "Mistral has generally lagged US rivals on model performance, revenue and release frequency, but in September raised a $3.3 billion round at a $24 billion valuation and its earnings have reportedly increased 20-fold in about a year.",
      "sources": [
        "WIRED"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "Earnings growth is 'reportedly'."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "B2",
      "text": "Growing US-Europe tension and the US restrictions on frontier model distribution have strengthened the case for European 'AI sovereignty'.",
      "sources": [
        "WIRED",
        "TechCrunch"
      ],
      "claim_by": null,
      "notes": [
        "TechCrunch cites Macron's 'third way in AI'."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "quotes": [
    {
      "id": "Q1",
      "text": "Mistral is still in the race of getting the best model. This is the main message.",
      "speaker": "Guillaume Lample",
      "speaker_id": "S2",
      "where": "Interview with WIRED",
      "via": [
        "WIRED"
      ],
      "single_source": true,
      "cut_off": false,
      "notes": [
        "Original WIRED text: “Mistral is still in the race of getting the best model,” Lample says. “This is the main message.”"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q2",
      "text": "Sometimes, people like to [make a big deal] over the US, versus Europe, versus China. But what really matters is to own the model—even for US companies. If you use a closed model, there is no guarantee it will still be there tomorrow.",
      "speaker": "Guillaume Lample",
      "speaker_id": "S2",
      "where": "Interview with WIRED",
      "via": [
        "WIRED"
      ],
      "single_source": true,
      "cut_off": false,
      "notes": [
        "Bracketed words are WIRED's editing."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q3",
      "text": "In the meantime, we’ll work with trusted partners and governments to make sure that the open source weights can be used to defend, but not to [perform] malicious attacks,",
      "speaker": "Pierre Stock",
      "speaker_id": "S3",
      "where": "Told TechCrunch",
      "via": [
        "TechCrunch"
      ],
      "single_source": true,
      "cut_off": false,
      "notes": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Q4",
      "text": "which is two to three times less than our Chinese competitors, and significantly less than the closed source competitors,",
      "speaker": "Pierre Stock",
      "speaker_id": "S3",
      "where": "Told TechCrunch, about 4,000 Nvidia GPUs used",
      "via": [
        "TechCrunch"
      ],
      "single_source": true,
      "cut_off": false,
      "notes": [
        "Partial quote as printed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Q5",
      "text": "The continental strategy of the EU to become more technologically sovereign … and the increased hostility of the US is a magic formula that all of a sudden puts Mistral—whose performance has not been spectacular—in a favorable position,",
      "speaker": "Andrea Renda",
      "speaker_id": "S4",
      "where": "Told WIRED in July",
      "via": [
        "WIRED"
      ],
      "single_source": true,
      "cut_off": false,
      "notes": [
        "Independent expert; ellipsis in original."
      ]
    }
  ],
  "numbers": [
